    "notes": {
        "715811cd-13e4-4b3f-a1db-10b37a73205e": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 400,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 224,
            "content": "## ⏱ Trigger test\n\nThe trigger registers its Attio webhook when the flow starts. The provoke lane waits 1 minute (do not remove the Wait) and then creates a company and adds it to the list. The trigger lane asserts the event and cleans up. Run this flow alone: other flows creating the same kind of data at the same time would also fire the trigger."
        },
        "79e978bd-b218-426f-9bf8-735860a63ad8": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 660,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 224,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption\n\nThis flow needs a **list with the API slug `e2e_attio_companies` whose parent object is Companies**. Attio has no API to delete lists, so the flow does not create one per run.\n\nSetup (once per workspace): Attio → Lists → *New list* → name it \"E2E Attio Companies\", choose **Companies**, then in the list settings set the API slug to `e2e_attio_companies`."
        }
    }
